fixtures/
venv/
.venv/
work/
# LOC download cache (loc.py disk cache incl. golden-testbed jp2 masters);
# machine-local and politely re-fetchable — never commit
cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/
reference-src/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.review-tmp/
# The published pages: one directory per city (viewer/<city-slug>/manifest.json
# plus that city's staged story images and its share card) and the index the
# page reads to resolve which to load. Generated by `viewer-manifest` /
# `publish` / `make_og_card.py`; only the loose page files and vendor/ are
# tracked. The card is ignored rather than committed because it is one CITY's:
# a tracked one at the viewer root would show one city's map to a reader
# sharing another's.
viewer/*/manifest.json
viewer/*/story-assets
viewer/*/og.jpg
viewer/cities.json
# The site-wide path builds wrote before the per-city split. Nothing writes it
# now, but a checkout from before the split still has one, and the page loads a
# lone manifest in a directory with no index, so leaving it untracked invites
# both a stray commit and a stale page.
viewer/manifest.json
# deploy/ holds the publishable bundle + the served tiles (deploy/tiles/*,
# provenance-labeled by directory); nothing under it is tracked
deploy/**
.hypothesis/
# the frontend linter's dev-only toolchain (make setup-js); package.json and
# package-lock.json ARE tracked, the tree they install is not
node_modules/
# agent session state, per-agent worktrees, and local scratch — machine-local,
# and nothing under it has ever been tracked
.claude/
# tool-created analysis caches (lint-imports); untracked, and they used to ride
# into the container build context
.grimp_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.env
*local.md
todo.md

# The lab notebook. Both trees and the three root files stay on disk and stay
# authoritative for the work; what changes is who can read them. The three
# named harnesses are libraries the tracked tests load, so they stay tracked —
# git will not re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, which is why
# this is `experiments/*` with exceptions rather than `experiments/`.
planning_docs/
ROADMAP.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
scripts/experiments/*
!scripts/experiments/numeral_rules.py
!scripts/experiments/qualification.py
!scripts/experiments/water.py
